\":0.55,\"zoom\":210}},\"plan-room-details\":{\"src\":\"/portfolio/media/f75b9a4592e2fc62e00e.webp\",\"width\":960,\"height\":655,\"alt\":\"Plan Room file details with tags\",\"context\":\"\\u003cp>\\u003cstrong>Tag-based organization, not folder trees.\\u003c/strong> The Plan Room, where CAD files, submittals, building plans, and site documents live, uses tags rather than a deep folder hierarchy. Tags carry color identity, audit metadata, and a description, so a customer can find what they need without remembering whose computer it was filed on. The same tag system surfaces in Folder Details and in the Show in Plan Room cross-reference, so it works everywhere the user might look.\\u003c/p>\",\"focus\":{\"x\":0.47,\"y\":0.24,\"zoom\":180}},\"tag-system\":{\"src\":\"/portfolio/media/21f229083be54fe87c14.webp\",\"width\":960,\"height\":461,\"alt\":\"Tag administration screen\",\"context\":\"\\u003cp>Across the redesign and the year of feature work that followed, the scope spanned the SiteMap canvas itself, the Plan Room file system, sewer and line detail with embedded inspection video and PACP observation codes, Reality Capture for point clouds and 3D scans, subscription management for the business customers, an admin surface covering tags, user management, training, and messaging, multi-tier permissions, the settings layer that controls map performance, and on-canvas annotation tools.\\u003c/p>\",\"focus\":{\"x\":0.23,\"y\":0.64,\"zoom\":190}},\"line-panel\":{\"src\":\"/portfolio/media/4cfcec7ea56659dc70a6.webp\",\"width\":346,\"height\":744,\"alt\":\"Actual Sewer Panel interface excerpt\"}}</script>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<section id=\"einstein-case-study\" hidden aria-label=\"Einstein Bros. Bagels case study\"><header class=\"eb-header\"><a href=\"/\" data-logo-home class=\"case-home-logo cursor-interaction\" aria-label=\"Josh Cole — home\"><img src=\"data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20viewBox%3D%2232%20