%20401.5L175.5%20401.98L176.18%20401.5ZM480.5%20411.25L480.25%20411.5L480.5%20411.85L480.9%20411.5Z%22%2F%3E%0A%3C%2Fsvg%3E%0A\" width=\"94\" height=\"52\" alt=\"Josh Cole signature\"></a><a href=\"/#case-studies\" data-return-case class=\"cursor-interaction\">← Case studies</a><span>UNION STATION HOTEL / MID–2010s</span></header><main><section class=\"ac-hotel-hero\"><figure class=\"ac-hotel-cover xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-atrium.webp\" width=\"1440\" height=\"810\" alt=\"Union Station Hotel’s renovated lobby atrium\" ></figure><div class=\"ac-hotel-hero-copy\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">NASHVILLE / CREATIVE DIRECTION & BRAND STRATEGY</span><h1>Union<br><em>Station.</em></h1><div class=\"ac-hotel-intro\"><span>HOTEL / NASHVILLE</span><p>A brand woven into the place.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"ac-hotel-anchor xc-pad\"><div class=\"ac-hotel-anchor-copy\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">ONE MARK / EVERY SCALE</span><h2>Before<br>you even<br><em>check in.</em></h2><p>From the entrance mosaic to an embroidered cuff, the identity belongs to the building.</p></div><figure class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-tile-mosaic.webp\" width=\"853\" height=\"531\" alt=\"USH monogram built into the hotel entrance mosaic\" ><figcaption><span>THE ENTRANCE / THE IDENTITY IS PART OF THE FLOOR</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-tile-mosaic.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"USH monogram built into the hotel entrance mosaic\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure></section><section class=\"ac-hotel-details xc-pad\"><div class=\"xc-section-heading\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">FOLLOW THE IDENTITY THROUGH THE HOTEL</span><h2>A sense<br><em>of belonging.</em></h2></div><div class=\"ac-gallery\" data-ac-gallery=\"hotel\"><div class=\"ac-gallery-choices\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Explore Union Station brand applications\"><button type=\"button\" data-ac-choice=\"entrance\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"cursor-interaction\"><span>01</span>The entrance</button><button type=\"button\" data-ac-choice=\"cuff\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"cursor-interaction\"><span>02</span>The smallest detail</button><button type=\"button\" data-ac-choice=\"street\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"cursor-interaction\"><span>03</span>The street</button><button type=\"button\" data-ac-choice=\"stay\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"cursor-interaction\"><span>04</span>The stay</button></div><figure class=\"xc-media ac-gallery-art\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-tile-mosaic.webp\" width=\"853\" height=\"531\" alt=\"The monogram designed into the entrance floor.\" data-ac-image><figcaption><span data-ac-caption role=\"status\">The monogram designed into the entrance floor.</span><button type=\"button\" data-ac-inspect class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure><script type=\"application/json\" data-ac-gallery-data>{\"entrance\":{\"title\":\"The entrance\",\"caption\":\"The monogram designed into the entrance floor.\",\"src\":\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-tile-mosaic.webp\",\"width\":853,\"height\":531},\"cuff\":{\"title\":\"The smallest detail\",\"caption\":\"The same monogram, embroidered on a staff cuff.\",\"src\":\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-monogram-cuff.webp\",\"width\":1424,\"height\":801},\"street\":{\"title\":\"The street\",\"caption\":\"Custom typographic sculpture, fabricated from the team’s design.\",\"src\":\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-sign-sculpture.webp\",\"width\":826,\"height\":1033},\"stay\":{\"title\":\"The stay\",\"caption\":\"A connected identity across uniforms, stationery and room service.\",\"src\":\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-uniform-room-service.webp\",\"width\":1600,\"height\":1091}}</script></div></section><article class=\"xc-story\"><section id=\"union-station-introduction\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-0\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">01 / UNION-STATION</span><h2>The brief</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-1\">Nashville in the mid-2010s was filling up fast. New hotels were opening constantly, tourism was accelerating, and the city's hospitality market was getting crowded. Union Station had something none of the new builds had. A 125-year-old Gothic train station on Broadway, a soaring lobby atrium, a history that predated the city's modern identity. The question was how to make that clear, coherent, and competitive in a market that was suddenly paying attention.</p><p style=\"grid-row:3\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-2\">The hotel had just completed a full interior renovation and wanted a brand to match. I was at ST8MNT and co-led the engagement as Creative Director and Brand Strategist, alongside a second creative director and a second strategist, with two art directors and a designer on the team.</p><figure style=\"grid-row:4\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-atrium.webp\" width=\"1440\" height=\"810\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"The lobby atrium after renovation\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-3\">The lobby atrium after renovation</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-atrium.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"The lobby atrium after renovation\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"union-station-the-anchor\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-1\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">02 / UNION-STATION</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-4\">The anchor</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-5\">The strategic anchor we landed on after discovery was the monogram. A single USH mark designed to live everywhere. The logic was that a hotel with this much physical presence needed a brand that worked the same way. Not a logo applied to things. A mark woven into the place itself.</p><figure style=\"grid-row:3\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-monogram-cuff.webp\" width=\"1424\" height=\"801\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"USH monogram embroidered on a staff cuff\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-6\">USH monogram embroidered on a staff cuff</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-monogram-cuff.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"USH monogram embroidered on a staff cuff\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"union-station-the-system\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-2\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">03 / UNION-STATION</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-7\">The system</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-8\">Everything followed from that decision. The color system pulled from the building's own materials and history. Chambray Blue, Palliser Copper, the warmth of aged brass and dark wood.</p><figure style=\"grid-row:3\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-palette.webp\" width=\"1440\" height=\"810\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Color system: Chambray Blue, Palliser Copper, brass, dark wood\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-9\">Color system: Chambray Blue, Palliser Copper, brass, dark wood</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-palette.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Color system: Chambray Blue, Palliser Copper, brass, dark wood\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure><p style=\"grid-row:4\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-10\">The primary typeface, Fortescue, brought the historical weight the architecture deserved, with GT Pressura Mono as the secondary face.</p><figure style=\"grid-row:5\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-type.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Fortescue as the primary typeface, GT Pressura Mono as the secondary\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-11\">Fortescue as the primary typeface, GT Pressura Mono as the secondary</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-type.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Fortescue as the primary typeface, GT Pressura Mono as the secondary\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure><figure style=\"grid-row:6\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-logo-lockup.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"844\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Primary logo with the clock tower illustration, and the lockup alternates\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-12\">Primary logo with the clock tower illustration, and the lockup alternates</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-logo-lockup.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Primary logo with the clock tower illustration, and the lockup alternates\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure><figure style=\"grid-row:7\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-uniform-room-service.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1091\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Uniform details, bow tie, tie bar, monogram buttons and suspenders, with the stationery folder and room service menu\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-13\">Uniform details, bow tie, tie bar, monogram buttons and suspenders, with the stationery folder and room service menu</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-uniform-room-service.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Uniform details, bow tie, tie bar, monogram buttons and suspenders, with the stationery folder and room service menu\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure><p style=\"grid-row:8\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-14\">The tile mosaic at the entrance was designed by our team and executed by the renovation contractor, so the brand was built into the building's floor before a guest ever checked in.</p><p style=\"grid-row:9\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-15\">And out front, a custom typographic sculpture, over six feet tall and fabricated from our design, put the wordmark in the street, visible from Broadway, part of the hotel's physical presence in the city.</p><figure style=\"grid-row:10\" class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-sign-sculpture.webp\" width=\"826\" height=\"1033\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Typographic sculpture on Broadway\"><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-16\">Typographic sculpture on Broadway</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/union-station-ush-sign-sculpture.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Typographic sculpture on Broadway\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure></section><section id=\"union-station-the-result\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-3\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">04 / UNION-STATION</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-17\">The result</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-18\">A brand system deep enough to dress a hotel from the sidewalk to the staff uniform to the room service menu.</p><p style=\"grid-row:3\" data-extended-source=\"union-station-source-19\">Years on, the mosaic is still in the floor and the sculpture is still on Broadway. Hospitality brands get refreshed every few years. The parts of this one that were built into the building are still doing their job.</p></section></article><footer class=\"xc-footer\"><span>UNION STATION HOTEL / JOSH COLE</span><a href=\"/#case-studies\" data-return-case class=\"cursor-interaction\">← Back to case studies</a></footer></main><dialog class=\"xc-inspector\"><div class=\"xc-inspector-toolbar\"><span data-xc-inspector-caption></span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspector-close class=\"cursor-interaction\">Close ✕</button></div><label class=\"xc-inspector-zoom\">Image scale <output data-xc-zoom-label>100%</output><input type=\"range\" min=\"100\" max=\"220\" step=\"10\" value=\"100\" data-xc-zoom aria-label=\"Image scale\"></label><div class=\"xc-inspector-pan\"><img data-xc-inspector-image alt=\"\"></div></dialog></section>\r\n<section id=\"nemo-case-study\" class=\"xc-case xc-nemo\" hidden aria-label=\"NEMO brand case study\"><header class=\"xc-header\"><a href=\"/\" data-logo-home class=\"case-home-logo cursor-interaction\" aria-label=\"Josh Cole — home\"><img src=\"data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20viewBox%3D%2232%2061%20685%20378%22%20role%3D%22img%22%20aria-labelledby%3D%22signature-title%20signature-desc%22%3E%0A%3Ctitle%20id%3D%22signature-title%22%3EJosh%20Cole%20signature%3C%2Ftitle%3E%0A%3Cdesc%20id%3D%22signature-desc%22%3EVector%20outline%20traced%20from%20Josh%20Cole's%20original%20handwritten%20signature.%20Irregular%20stroke%20edges%20retained.%3C%2Fdesc%3E%0A%3Cmetadata%3EDerived%20from%20josh-cole-art-logo.png%3B%20SHA256%2079df3f9bac1896a3d01003663dda481c6fb0a288c4a47e22bb28b6b6d937916d.%20Alpha%20contour%20127.5%3B%20simplification%20tolerance%200.16%20source%20pixels.%20Gradient%20reconstructed%20from%20source%20colours.%3C%2Fmetadata%3E%0A%3Cpath%20fill%3D%22%23e63946%22%20fill-rule%3D%22evenodd%22%20d%3D%22M404.5%2066.44L403.1%2067.5L401.37%2070.5L401.2%2071.5L401.37%2081.5L404.02%2097.5L404.78%20100.5L405.15%20103.5L405.58%20104.5L405.37%20105.5L405.69%20106.5L406.15%20112.5L407.84%20118.5L408.24%20124.5L408.78%20126.5L409.17%20130.5L409.71%20131.5L410.06%20137.5L410.47%2