\"novensia\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">The system behind Novensia ↗</a></div></section><section class=\"ns-em-lab xc-pad\"><div class=\"xc-section-heading\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">INTERACTIVE RULE SPECIMEN</span><h2>Two states.<br><em>One clear read.</em></h2><p>Change the context. See where gold and coral belong.</p></div><div class=\"ns-em-context\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Emergence color context\"><button type=\"button\" data-em-context=\"canvas\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Node canvas</button><button type=\"button\" data-em-context=\"interface\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Product interface</button></div><div class=\"ns-em-lab-grid\"><div class=\"ns-em-specimen\"><div data-em-node-controls class=\"ns-em-toggles\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-em-running checked> Running</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-em-selected> Selected</label></div><div data-em-node class=\"ns-em-node\" data-running=\"true\" data-selected=\"false\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Running node, not selected\"><span class=\"ns-em-node-status\" data-em-node-status>RUNNING</span><h3>Voice profile</h3><div><span>Temperature</span><code>0.7</code></div></div><div data-em-interface class=\"ns-em-interface\" hidden><span class=\"ns-em-brand-dot\">Brand accent</span><span class=\"ns-em-primary-sample\">Primary action</span><span class=\"ns-em-secondary-sample\">Secondary accent</span></div><p class=\"ns-em-specimen-note\">A demonstration of the design rule, using example content.</p></div><div class=\"ns-em-rule-copy\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\" data-em-rule-label>ON THE CANVAS</span><h3 data-em-rule-title>State on the node.<br>Selection around it.</h3><p data-em-rule-description>Gold marks a running node. Coral marks the selection ring. The two states can be visible together without competing.</p><dl><div><dt>Gold</dt><dd>#E0A33E</dd></div><div><dt>Coral</dt><dd>#EE7F4E</dd></div></dl></div></div></section><section class=\"ns-em-type xc-pad\"><div class=\"xc-section-heading\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">TYPE AS CATEGORY</span><h2>Before you read it,<br><em>you know what it is.</em></h2></div><div class=\"ns-em-type-row\"><span>01 / INTERFACE / GEIST SANS</span><p class=\"ns-em-ui-type\">Temperature</p><small>A label a human wrote.</small></div><div class=\"ns-em-type-row\"><span>02 / CONTENT / NEWSREADER</span><p class=\"ns-em-content-type\">Something new forming out of something larger.</p><small>The writing stays distinct from the interface.</small></div><div class=\"ns-em-type-row\"><span>03 / MACHINE VALUES / GEIST MONO</span><p class=\"ns-em-machine-type\">0.7</p><small>A value the machine produced.</small></div></section><article class=\"xc-story\"><section id=\"emergence-introduction\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-0\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">01 / EMERGENCE</span><h2>The brief</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-1\">Emergence is the design system that assembles to create Novensia. It's named for what it's meant to do. Give one idea a visual form. <em>Something new forming out of something larger.</em></p><figure style=\"grid-row:3\" data-cw-original=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections.webp\" data-case-motion-static class=\"cw-composition cw-system xc-media\"><div class=\"cw-sequence cw-screens\" data-cw-sequence><div class=\"cw-sequence-nav\"><span>SCREEN DETAILS / <output data-cw-position>01 / 04</output></span><div><button type=\"button\" data-cw-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous panel\">←</button><button type=\"button\" data-cw-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next panel\">→</button></div></div><div id=\"cw-emergence-reference\" class=\"cw-rail\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Source image details; scroll sideways\"><div class=\"cw-tile\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cw-art\" data-cw-open=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-1.webp\" data-cw-caption=\"Color and semantic state\" aria-label=\"View Color and semantic state full width\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-1.webp\" width=\"385\" height=\"604\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Color and semantic state\"></button><span class=\"cw-tile-label\">01 / Color and semantic state <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></span></div><div class=\"cw-tile\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cw-art\" data-cw-open=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-2.webp\" data-cw-caption=\"Typography\" aria-label=\"View Typography full width\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-2.webp\" width=\"385\" height=\"604\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Typography\"></button><span class=\"cw-tile-label\">02 / Typography <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></span></div><div class=\"cw-tile\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cw-art\" data-cw-open=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-3.webp\" data-cw-caption=\"Components\" aria-label=\"View Components full width\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-3.webp\" width=\"387\" height=\"604\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Components\"></button><span class=\"cw-tile-label\">03 / Components <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></span></div><div class=\"cw-tile\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"cw-art\" data-cw-open=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-4.webp\" data-cw-caption=\"Readouts and node states\" aria-label=\"View Readouts and node states full width\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections-detail-4.webp\" width=\"386\" height=\"604\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Readouts and node states\"></button><span class=\"cw-tile-label\">04 / Readouts and node states <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption><span data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-2\">The System</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-system-sections.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"The System\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">View complete image ↗</button></figcaption></figure><p style=\"grid-row:4\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-3\">Content is what the product is for. The whole system is dark-mode-first by intent, not by user preference. Dark is what lets warm read as warm and lets the content sit above everything else.</p><p style=\"grid-row:5\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-4\">The system came before the product. The thesis showed up before the name did, which is why the tokens are named for the idea, not the product. Novensia sits on top of it. The system underneath doesn't depend on it.</p></section><section id=\"emergence-one-rule-two-contexts\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-1\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">02 / EMERGENCE</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-5\">One rule, two contexts</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-6\">The system runs on gold and coral, and one rule governs them. Gold and coral split by context. On the node canvas, gold means <em>running</em> and coral means <em>selected</em>, so state lives on the node and interaction lives in a ring around it. Different layers, no collision. A node can be running and selected at once. Everywhere else, gold is the primary brand accent and coral is the secondary. One rule, applied two ways, holds the whole system together.</p><p style=\"grid-row:3\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-7\">The grays carry a deliberate blue-violet bias, not neutral. That bias is what makes the warm accents read as truly hot. And gold gets used sparingly. Roughly three touches per screen, the brand mark, the primary action, the active step. Restraint is what makes it read as <em>the</em> accent instead of decoration.</p></section><section id=\"emergence-type-as-category\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-2\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">03 / EMERGENCE</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-8\">Type as category</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-9\">Three typefaces, three jobs. Geist Sans for interface (labels, controls, headings). Newsreader for content (your writing samples and the drafts, and nothing else). Geist Mono for machine values (model strings, temperatures, scores, JSON).</p><p style=\"grid-row:3\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-10\">The rule that decides between them. A label is a word a human wrote (&quot;Temperature&quot;). A value is data the machine produced (&quot;0.7&quot;). Label gets Geist. Value gets Mono. The reader knows what kind of thing they're looking at before they read a word of it.</p><p style=\"grid-row:4\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-11\">Two weights across all three faces, regular and medium. Emphasis comes from size, color, and the step between them, never a third weight.</p></section><section id=\"emergence-discipline\" class=\"xc-chapter xc-chapter-3\"><span class=\"xc-chapter-index\" aria-hidden=\"true\">04 / EMERGENCE</span><h2 data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-12\">Discipline</h2><p style=\"grid-row:2\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-13\">The system's point of view is mostly about restraint.</p><p style=\"grid-row:3\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-14\">Gold touches about three things per screen. Two type weights, never three. Grays stay blue-violet-biased, never neutral. Red borders use a deep, desaturated red, because full-strength red on the void buzzes. It's reserved for dots, fills, and text where it carries a signal. Each of these is a limit, and they all protect the same thing. The content stays brightest, the accent stays the accent, nothing competes with what the user came to make.</p><p style=\"grid-row:4\" data-extended-source=\"emergence-source-15\">The system is built from real primitives. The brand mark, the coral focus state, the gold button. Assembled from the same parts, no decoration bolted on.</p></section></article><section class=\"ns-evidence ns-em-reference xc-pad\"><div class=\"xc-section-heading\"><span class=\"xc-eyebrow\">THE ACTUAL SYSTEM REFERENCE</span><h2>Restraint,<br><em>made explicit.</em></h2></div><figure class=\"xc-media\"><img src=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-emergence-01.webp\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Original Emergence color reference: surfaces, gold, coral and their roles.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><span>Original Emergence color reference: surfaces, gold, coral and their roles.</span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspect=\"/portfolio/case-assets/emergence-emergence-01.webp\" data-xc-caption=\"Original Emergence color reference: surfaces, gold, coral and their roles.\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Inspect the work ↗</button></figcaption></figure></section><aside class=\"ns-em-crosslink\"><span>FROM THE SYSTEM TO THE PRODUCT</span><a href=\"/work/novensia\" data-open-case=\"novensia\" class=\"cursor-interaction\">Explore Novensia ↗</a></aside><footer class=\"xc-footer\"><span>EMERGENCE / JOSH COLE</span><a href=\"/#case-studies\" data-return-case class=\"cursor-interaction\">← Back to case studies</a></footer></main><dialog class=\"xc-inspector\"><div class=\"xc-inspector-toolbar\"><span data-xc-inspector-caption></span><button type=\"button\" data-xc-inspector-close class=\"cursor-interaction\">Close ✕</button></div><label class=\"xc-inspector-zoom\">Image scale <output data-xc-zoom-label>100%</output><input type=\"range\" min=\"100\" max=\"220\" step=\"10\" value=\"100\" data-xc-zoom aria-label=\"Image scale\"></label><div class=\"xc-inspector-pan\"><img data-xc-inspector-image alt=\"\"></div></dialog></section>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<script id=\"codex-visualization-tabs\">\r\n(() => {\r\n  const selector = '.nav[role=\"tablist\"] [role=\"tab\"]';\r\n  const disabled = ':disabled,[aria-disabled=\"true\"]';\r\n  const selectTab = (selected) => {\r\n    const panelId = selected.getAttribute(\"aria-controls\");\r\n    for (const tab of selected.closest('[role=\"tablist\"]').querySelectorAll('[role=\"tab\"]')) {\r\n      const active = tab === selected;\r\n      tab.classList.toggle(\"active\", active);\r\n      tab.setAttribute(\"aria-selected\", String(active));\r\n      const id = tab.getAttribute(\"aria-controls\");\r\n      const panel = id && document.getElementById(id);\r\n      if (panel != null) {\r\n        panel.hidden = id !== panelId;\r\n        if (!panel.hidden && selected.id) {\r\n          panel.setAttribute(\"aria-labelledby\", selected.id);\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n  const interact = (event) => {\r\n    const tab = event.target?.closest?.(selector);\r\n    if (event.defaultPrevented || tab == null || tab.matches(disabled)) {\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    if (event.type === \"click\") {\r\n      selectTab(tab);\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    const tabs = Array.from(\r\n      tab.closest('[role=\"tablist\"]').querySelectorAll('[role=\"tab\"]'),\r\n    ).filter((candidate) => !candidate.matches(disabled));\r\n    const current = tabs.indexOf(tab);\r\n    let next;\r\n    if (event.key === \"ArrowRight\" || event.key === \"ArrowDown\") {\r\n      next = (current + 1) % tabs.length;\r\n    } else if (event.key === \"ArrowLeft\" || event.key === \"ArrowUp\") {\r\n      next = (current + tabs.length - 1) % tabs.length;\r\n    } else if (event.key === \"Home\") {\r\n      next = 0;\r\n    } else if (event.key === \"End\") {\r\n      next = tabs.length - 1;\r\n    } else {\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    tabs[next].focus();\r\n    selectTab(tabs[next]);\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  for (const list of document.querySelectorAll('.nav[role=\"tablist\"]')) {\r\n    const selected =\r\n      list.querySelector('[role=\"tab\"][aria-selected=\"true\"]') ??\r\n      list.querySelector('[role=\"tab\"].active') ??\r\n      list.querySelector('[role=\"tab\"]');\r\n    if (selected != null) {\r\n      selectTab(selected);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  document.addEventListener(\"click\", interact);\r\n  document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", interact);\r\n  window.addEventListener(\"pagehide\", () => {\r\n    document.removeEventListener(\"click\", interact);\r\n    document.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", interact);\r\n  }, { once: true });\r\n})();\r\n</script>\r\n<script id=\"codex-visualization-carousel\">\r\n  (() => {\r\n    for (const root of document.querySelectorAll(\".viz-carousel\")) {\r\n      const panels = Array.from(\r\n        root.querySelectorAll(\":scope > [data-variant]\"),\r\n      );\r\n      if (panels.length === 0) {\r\n        continue;\r\n      }\r\n      root.setAttribute(\"role\", \"group\");\r\n      panels.forEach((panel, index) => {\r\n        panel.hidden = index !== 0;\r\n        panel.setAttribute(\"role\", \"group\");\r\n        if (!panel.hasAttribute(\"aria-label\")) {\r\n          panel.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", panel.dataset.variant);\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n      root.dataset.activeVariant = panels[0].dataset.variant;\r\n      if (panels.length === 1) {\r\n        continue;\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      const controls = document.createElement(\"div\");\r\n      controls.className = \"viz-carousel-controls\";\r\n      // Portable copy of the settings dropdown's legacy glyph; no 14px icon-package preset matches it.\r\n      // https://github.com/openai/openai/blob/master/codex/codex-apps/webview/src/icons/chevron.svg\r\n      controls.innerHTML = `\r\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"viz-carousel-previous cursor-interaction\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-left\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m15 18-6-6 6-6\"></path></svg></button>\r\n      <details class=\"viz-carousel-picker\">\r\n        <summary class=\"cursor-interaction\">\r\n          <span class=\"viz-carousel-count tabular-nums\"></span>\r\n          <span class=\"viz-carousel-name\"></span>\r\n          <svg class=\"viz-carousel-caret\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 21\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\r\n            <path d=\"M15.2793 7.71101C15.539 7.45131 15.961 7.45131 16.2207 7.71101C16.4804 7.97071 16.4804 8.39272 16.2207 8.65242L10.4707 14.4024C10.211 14.6621 9.78902 14.6621 9.52932 14.4024L3.77932 8.65242L3.69436 8.54792C3.52385 8.28979 3.55205 7.93828 3.77932 7.71101C4.00659 7.48374 4.3581 7.45554 4.61623 7.62605L4.72073 7.71101L10 12.9903L15.2793 7.71101Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" />\r\n          </svg>\r\n        </summary>\r\n        <div class=\"viz-carousel-options\"></div>\r\n      </details>\r\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"viz-carousel-next cursor-interaction\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></button>`;\r\n      const previous = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-previous\");\r\n      const next = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-next\");\r\n      const picker = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-picker\");\r\n      const summary = picker.querySelector(\"summary\");\r\n      const count = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-count\");\r\n      const name = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-name\");\r\n      const options = controls.querySelector(\".viz-carousel-options\");\r\n      const status = document.createElement(\"span\");\r\n      status.className = \"sr-only\";\r\n      status.setAttribute(\"role\", \"status\");\r\n      status.setAttribute(\"aria-live\", \"polite\");\r\n      status.setAttribute(\"aria-atomic\", \"true\");\r\n      previous.setAttribute(\r\n        \"aria-label\",\r\n        root.dataset.previousLabel ?? \"Previous variant\",\r\n      );\r\n      next.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", root.dataset.nextLabel ?? \"Next variant\");\r\n\r\n      let active = 0;\r\n      let mousePointerId = null;\r\n      let summaryPointerHandled = false;\r\n      summary.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", (event) => {\r\n        summaryPointerHandled =\r\n          event.pointerType === \"mouse\" && event.button === 0 && !event.ctrlKey;\r\n        if (!summaryPointerHandled) {\r\n          return;\r\n        }\r\n        event.preventDefault();\r\n        summary.focus({ preventScroll: true });\r\n        picker.open = !picker.open;\r\n        mousePointerId = picker.open ? event.pointerId : null;\r\n      });\r\n      summary.addEventListener(\"click\", (event) => {\r\n        if (summaryPointerHandled && event.detail > 0) {\r\n          event.preventDefault();\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n      const choices = panels.map((panel, index) => {\r\n        const choice = document.createElement(\"button\");\r\n        choice.type = \"button\";\r\n        choice.className = \"cursor-interaction\";\r\n        choice.textContent = panel.dataset.variant;\r\n        choice.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\r\n          select(index);\r\n          summary.focus();\r\n        });\r\n        choice.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", (event) => {\r\n          if (\r\n            picker.open &&\r\n            event.pointerType === \"mouse\" &&\r\n            event.button === 0 &&\r\n            event.pointerId === mousePointerId\r\n          ) {\r\n            choice.click();\r\n          }\r\n        });\r\n        options.appendChild(choice);\r\n        return choice;\r\n      });\r\n      const select = (index) => {\r\n        const changed = active !== index;\r\n        active = index;\r\n        panels.forEach((panel, position) => {\r\n          panel.hidden = position !== active;\r\n          choices[position].setAttribute(\r\n            \"aria-current\",\r\n            String(position === active),\r\n          );\r\n        });\r\n        root.dataset.activeVariant = panels[active].dataset.variant;\r\n        count.textContent = `${active + 1} / ${panels.length}`;\r\n        name.textContent = panels[active].dataset.variant;\r\n        picker.open = false;\r\n        mousePointerId = null;\r\n        if (changed) {\r\n          status.textContent = `${count.textContent}: ${name.textContent}`;\r\n        }\r\n      };\r\n      previous.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n        select((active + panels.length - 1) % panels.length),\r\n      );\r\n      next.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n        select((active + 1) % panels.length),\r\n      );\r\n      picker.addEventListener(\"keydown\", (event) => {\r\n        if (event.key === \"Escape\" && picker.open) {\r\n          event.preventDefault();\r\n          picker.open = false;\r\n          mousePointerId = null;\r\n          summary.focus();\r\n          return;\r\n        }\r\n        if (event.altKey || event.ctrlKey || event.metaKey) {\r\n          return;\r\n        }\r\n        const index = choices.indexOf(document.activeElement);\r\n        let nextIndex;\r\n        if (event.key === \"ArrowDown\") {\r\n          nextIndex = index < 0 ? active : (index + 1) % choices.length;\r\n        } else if (event.key === \"ArrowUp\") {\r\n          nextIndex = index < 0 ? active : (index + choices.length - 1) % choices.length;\r\n        } else if (picker.open && event.key === \"Home\") {\r\n          nextIndex = 0;\r\n        } else if (picker.open && event.key === \"End\") {\r\n          nextIndex = choices.length - 1;\r\n        } else {\r\n          return;\r\n        }\r\n        event.preventDefault();\r\n        picker.open = true;\r\n        choices[nextIndex].focus();\r\n      });\r\n      picker.addEventListener(\"focusout\", (event) => {\r\n        if (!picker.contains(event.relatedTarget)) {\r\n          picker.open = false;\r\n          mousePointerId = null;\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n      const dismiss = (event) => {\r\n        if (!summary.contains(event.target)) {\r\n          mousePointerId = null;\r\n        }\r\n        if (!picker.contains(event.target)) {\r\n          picker.open = false;\r\n        }\r\n      };\r\n      const endPointerSelection = () => {\r\n        mousePointerId = null;\r\n      };\r\n      const sizePicker = () => {\r\n        root.style.setProperty(\r\n          \"--viz-carousel-picker-height\",\r\n          `${picker.open ? options.offsetHeight : 0}px`,\r\n        );\r\n      };\r\n      picker.addEventListener(\"toggle\", sizePicker);\r\n      window.addEventListener(\"resize\", sizePicker);\r\n      document.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", dismiss);\r\n      document.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", endPointerSelection);\r\n      document.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", endPointerSelection);\r\n      window.addEventListener(\"blur\", endPointerSelection);\r\n      window.addEventListener(\r\n        \"pagehide\",\r\n        () => {\r\n          document.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", dismiss);\r\n          document.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", endPointerSelection);\r\n          document.removeEventListener(\"pointercancel\", endPointerSelection);\r\n          window.removeEventListener(\"blur\", endPointerSelection);\r\n          window.removeEventListener(\"resize\", sizePicker);\r\n        },\r\n        { once: true },\r\n      );\r\n      root.append(controls, status);\r\n      select(0);\r\n    }\r\n  })();\r\n</script>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<script defer src=\"/portfolio/site-77c6241f8594d13d.js\"></script></body>\r\n</html>\r\n"